-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II (sections 42 to 55.2(5.1)) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a worker, self-employed person, survivor, child or person with a disability who contributes to or may claim from the
-- Canada Pension Plan, asking whether they qualify for a retirement pension or a disability, survivor's or children's benefit,
-- how much it is, whether their earnings are divided on a divorce or separation, and what they may be made to repay; and a former
-- spouse or former common-law partner whose earnings may be divided. (What they must contribute is Part I's, pieces cp1 and cp2;
-- this layer asks no contribution question.)
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the cp3 modules imported above as questions the person asks about their own case. Nothing
-- here is new law and no rule is restated: each question builds what the rule needs from plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date) and calls the rule. A fact about the other party (the Minister, a court, a former partner) on which the text makes a right depend
-- is its own input, worded as the person would be told it ("Has the Minister determined ...?"). A judgment the Act leaves to the Minister is an
-- input supplied conditionally; no answer here decides it.
--
-- Where the rules ask for a list (the years of a record, the twelve Consumer Price Index figures) the question asks for the numbers the person can
-- state from their Statement of Contributions: how many years, how many months, the total, or each of the twelve figures. Where the text sets a figure
-- by regulation or by the Minister (the early-or-late factor of subsection 46(3.1), the Minister's factor of subsection 46(3)), the question asks for
-- the figure; this layer does not look it up.
-- No question is asked about the rules that need a list or a record of years or months, because the person cannot be asked for a list in one answer: the month-by-month
-- rules of sections 51 to 52.2, the sums of sections 50 to 50.2, the lookback years of sections 51.1, 51.2, 53.3 and 53.4, the multi-year annual adjustment of subsection
-- 45(2), the months of cohabitation of subsections 55(3) and 55.1(4), and the deductions of subsections 48(2) to (4) on a list of months. Each is encoded and tested in layer 1
-- (NOTES.md, coverage table), and the questions above and below take their totals as numbers. Nor is any question asked about the machinery (regulation-making powers).

§ `Canada Pension Plan Part II -- the questions of a contributor, survivor, child or former spouse or partner`

§§ `Who counts: contributor, disabled, survivor, child (sections 2(1), 42)`

-- s 2(1) "contributor". A contributor is someone who has made an employee's contribution, or a contribution on their own self-employed earnings, or
-- who has had earnings attributed to them by a division.
@export Am I a contributor under the Canada Pension Plan (s 2(1))?
GIVEN `I have made an employee's contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an employee's contribution to the Canada Pension Plan?
      `I have made a contribution on my own self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a contribution on your own self-employed earnings?
      `the most earnings on which a contribution was made for any one year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the largest amount of earnings, for any one year, on which a contribution was made under the Plan, in dollars? (0 if none)
      `earnings have been attributed to me by a division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have unadjusted pensionable earnings been attributed to you by a division on a divorce or separation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a contributor under the Canada Pension Plan` IF
    `s 2(1) — a contributor` `I have made an employee's contribution` `I have made a contribution on my own self-employed earnings` (LIST `the most earnings on which a contribution was made for any one year`) `earnings have been attributed to me by a division`

-- s 42(2)(a). A person is disabled for the Plan only if the Minister determines, in the prescribed manner, that they have a severe and prolonged
-- disability: severe means they cannot regularly pursue any substantially gainful occupation, prolonged means likely long continued and of
-- indefinite duration, or likely to result in death. The determination is the Minister's; the first input is that determination.
@export Am I considered disabled under the Canada Pension Plan (s 42(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the Minister has determined, in the prescribed manner, that I have a severe and prolonged mental or physical disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister determined, in the prescribed manner, that you have a severe and prolonged mental or physical disability?
      `my disability makes me incapable regularly of pursuing any substantially gainful occupation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your disability make you incapable of regularly pursuing any substantially gainful occupation?
      `it is determined in the prescribed manner that my disability is likely to be long continued and of indefinite duration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been determined, in the prescribed manner, that your disability is likely to be long continued and of indefinite duration?
      `it is determined in the prescribed manner that my disability is likely to result in death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been determined, in the prescribed manner, that your disability is likely to result in death?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I considered disabled under the Canada Pension Plan` IF
    `s 42(2)(a) — a person is considered to be disabled`
        `the Minister has determined, in the prescribed manner, that I have a severe and prolonged mental or physical disability`
        (`s 42(2)(a)(i) — a disability is severe` `my disability makes me incapable regularly of pursuing any substantially gainful occupation`)
        (`s 42(2)(a)(ii) — a disability is prolonged` `it is determined in the prescribed manner that my disability is likely to be long continued and of indefinite duration` `it is determined in the prescribed manner that my disability is likely to result in death`)

-- s 42(2)(b). From what time a person is deemed to have become disabled: the time the Minister determines, but never earlier than fifteen months
-- before the application was made.
@export From what date am I deemed to have become disabled (s 42(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the time the Minister determined, in the prescribed manner, that I became disabled` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Minister determine, in the prescribed manner, that you became disabled?
      `the day I made my application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make your application?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what date am I deemed to have become disabled` IS
    `s 42(2)(b) — the time a person is deemed to have become disabled` `the time the Minister determined, in the prescribed manner, that I became disabled` `the day I made my application`

-- s 42(1) "child of a contributor". The contributor's own child, a person adopted by the contributor under 21, or a person the contributor had parenting
-- time or decision-making responsibility for; not a child adopted by a stranger before the contributor's death or disability, unless the contributor was
-- maintaining the child.
@export Am I a child of the contributor under the Canada Pension Plan (s 42(1))?
GIVEN `I am the contributor's child, born before or after the contributor's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a child of the contributor, whether born before or after the contributor's death?
      `I was adopted by the contributor, legally or in fact, while under twenty-one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you adopted, legally or in fact, by the contributor while you were under twenty-one?
      `the contributor had parenting time or decision-making responsibility for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the contributor have, or immediately before you turned 21 did they have, parenting time or decision-making responsibility (as the Divorce Act defines it) for you, legally or in fact?
      `I was adopted by someone else before the contributor's death or disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you adopted, legally or in fact, by someone other than the contributor or their spouse or common-law partner before the contributor died or became disabled?
      `the contributor was maintaining me, as the regulations define` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contributor maintaining you, as the Regulations define maintaining a child (regulation 65.1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a child of the contributor under the Canada Pension Plan` IF
    `s 42(1) — a child of a contributor` `I am the contributor's child, born before or after the contributor's death` `I was adopted by the contributor, legally or in fact, while under twenty-one` `the contributor had parenting time or decision-making responsibility for me` `I was adopted by someone else before the contributor's death or disability` `the contributor was maintaining me, as the regulations define`

-- Not a question: the paragraph of the "dependent child" definition a person falls under, from the facts below. Used by the three questions that follow.
GIVEN `I am a child of the contributor under the Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE
      `I attend a school or university full time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I attend a school or university part time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have been disabled without interruption since I turned eighteen or the contributor died, whichever was later` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `cp3 Kind of dependent child`
`cp3 seat — the kind of dependent child I am` `I am a child of the contributor under the Plan` `my date of birth` `the date I am asking about` `I attend a school or university full time` `I attend a school or university part time` `I am disabled` `I have been disabled without interruption since I turned eighteen or the contributor died, whichever was later` MEANS
    `s 42(1) — the kind of dependent child that a child of a contributor is` `I am a child of the contributor under the Plan` `my date of birth` `the date I am asking about` `I attend a school or university full time` `I attend a school or university part time` `I am disabled` `I have been disabled without interruption since I turned eighteen or the contributor died, whichever was later`

-- s 42(1) "dependent child of a contributor": under 18; or 18 or more and under 25 and at school or university (regulation 66: full time, or at least 20 per cent of a course load); or 18 or more and
-- disabled without a break since the later of turning 18 and the contributor's death.
@export Am I a dependent child of the contributor under the Canada Pension Plan (s 42(1))?
GIVEN `I am a child of the contributor under the Plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a child of the contributor under the Plan (answer the question above)?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date are you asking whether you are a dependent child?
      `I attend a school or university full time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you attend a school or university full time, as the Regulations define (regulation 66)?
      `I attend a school or university part time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you attend a school or university part time, as the Regulations define (regulation 66)?
      `I am disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disabled under the Plan?
      `I have been disabled without interruption since I turned eighteen or the contributor died, whichever was later` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been disabled without interruption since you turned eighteen or the contributor died, whichever was later?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a dependent child of the contributor under the Canada Pension Plan` IF
    `s 42(1) — a dependent child of a contributor` (`cp3 seat — the kind of dependent child I am` `I am a child of the contributor under the Plan` `my date of birth` `the date I am asking about` `I attend a school or university full time` `I attend a school or university part time` `I am disabled` `I have been disabled without interruption since I turned eighteen or the contributor died, whichever was later`)

-- s 42(1) "orphan of a contributor": a dependent child (other than one only by paragraph (c)) of a contributor who has died.
@export Am I an orphan of the contributor under the Canada Pension Plan (s 42(1))?
GIVEN `I am a child of the contributor under the Plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a child of the contributor under the Plan?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date are you asking?
      `I attend a school or university full time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you attend a school or university full time, as the Regulations define?
      `I attend a school or university part time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you attend a school or university part time, as the Regulations define?
      `I am disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disabled under the Plan?
      `I have been disabled without interruption since I turned eighteen or the contributor died, whichever was later` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been disabled without interruption since you turned eighteen or the contributor died, whichever was later?
      `the contributor has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contributor died?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an orphan of the contributor under the Canada Pension Plan` IF
    `s 42(1) — an orphan of a contributor` (`cp3 seat — the kind of dependent child I am` `I am a child of the contributor under the Plan` `my date of birth` `the date I am asking about` `I attend a school or university full time` `I attend a school or university part time` `I am disabled` `I have been disabled without interruption since I turned eighteen or the contributor died, whichever was later`) `the contributor has died`

-- s 42(1) "disabled contributor's child": a dependent child (other than one only by paragraph (c)) of a contributor who is disabled.
@export Am I a disabled contributor's child under the Canada Pension Plan (s 42(1))?
GIVEN `I am a child of the contributor under the Plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a child of the contributor under the Plan?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date are you asking?
      `I attend a school or university full time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you attend a school or university full time, as the Regulations define?
      `I attend a school or university part time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you attend a school or university part time, as the Regulations define?
      `I am disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you yourself disabled under the Plan?
      `I have been disabled without interruption since I turned eighteen or the contributor died, whichever was later` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been disabled without interruption since you turned eighteen or the contributor died, whichever was later?
      `the contributor is disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contributor disabled under the Plan?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a disabled contributor's child under the Canada Pension Plan` IF
    `s 42(1) — a disabled contributor's child` (`cp3 seat — the kind of dependent child I am` `I am a child of the contributor under the Plan` `my date of birth` `the date I am asking about` `I attend a school or university full time` `I attend a school or university part time` `I am disabled` `I have been disabled without interruption since I turned eighteen or the contributor died, whichever was later`) `the contributor is disabled`

-- s 42(1) "survivor": the contributor's common-law partner at the time of death (a conjugal relationship of at least a year), or, only if the contributor had no
-- common-law partner then, the person married to the contributor at the time of death.
@export Am I a survivor of the contributor under the Canada Pension Plan (s 42(1))?
GIVEN `I was living with the contributor in a conjugal relationship when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you living with the contributor in a conjugal relationship when they died?
      `the day I began living with the contributor in that relationship` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you begin living with the contributor in that conjugal relationship? (Any date if you were not.)
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the contributor die?
      `I was married to the contributor when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you married to the contributor when they died?
      `someone was the contributor's common-law partner when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was anyone (you or someone else) the contributor's common-law partner when they died?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a survivor of the contributor under the Canada Pension Plan` IF
    `s 42(1) — a survivor of a deceased contributor`
        (`s 2(1) — a common-law partner of a contributor at the contributor's death` `I was living with the contributor in a conjugal relationship when they died` `the day I began living with the contributor in that relationship` `the day the contributor died`)
        `I was married to the contributor when they died`
        `someone was the contributor's common-law partner when they died`

-- s 42(1) "survivor with dependent children": a survivor who wholly or substantially maintains (regulation 65: more than 50 per cent of the maintenance of) at least one dependent child of the contributor.
@export Am I a survivor with dependent children under the Canada Pension Plan (s 42(1))?
GIVEN `I am a survivor of the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a survivor of the contributor under the Plan?
      `the number of the contributor's dependent children whom I wholly or substantially maintain` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the contributor's dependent children do you maintain wholly or substantially (more than 50 per cent of the maintenance, as the Regulations define: regulation 65)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a survivor with dependent children under the Canada Pension Plan` IF
    `s 42(1) — a survivor with dependent children` `I am a survivor of the contributor` `the number of the contributor's dependent children whom I wholly or substantially maintain`

-- s 42(1) "basic number of contributory months": 120 less the months excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability.
@export What is my basic number of contributory months (s 42(1))?
GIVEN `the number of months excluded from my contributory period by reason of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months have been excluded from your contributory period, under the Plan or a provincial plan, by reason of disability?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my basic number of contributory months` IS
    `s 42(1) — the basic number of contributory months` `the number of months excluded from my contributory period by reason of disability`

§§ `The Pension Index (section 43)`

-- s 43(1). The Pension Index for a year: the average of the twelve monthly Consumer Price Index figures for the twelve months ending on 31 October of the year before.
-- (Regulation 75 rounds the average to one decimal place; this answer is not rounded.)
@export What is the Pension Index for a year, from the twelve monthly Consumer Price Index figures (s 43(1))?
GIVEN `the Consumer Price Index for November` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Consumer Price Index for November, in the twelve months ending on 31 October of the year before the year you ask about?
      `the Consumer Price Index for December` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Consumer Price Index for December, in the twelve months ending on 31 October of the year before the year you ask about?
      `the Consumer Price Index for January` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Consumer Price Index for January, in the twelve months ending on 31 October of the year before the year you ask about?
      `the Consumer Price Index for February` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Consumer Price Index for February, in the twelve months ending on 31 October of the year before the year you ask about?
      `the Consumer Price Index for March` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Consumer Price Index for March, in the twelve months ending on 31 October of the year before the year you ask about?
      `the Consumer Price Index for April` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Consumer Price Index for April, in the twelve months ending on 31 October of the year before the year you ask about?
      `the Consumer Price Index for May` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Consumer Price Index for May, in the twelve months ending on 31 October of the year before the year you ask about?
      `the Consumer Price Index for June` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Consumer Price Index for June, in the twelve months ending on 31 October of the year before the year you ask about?
      `the Consumer Price Index for July` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Consumer Price Index for July, in the twelve months ending on 31 October of the year before the year you ask about?
      `the Consumer Price Index for August` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Consumer Price Index for August, in the twelve months ending on 31 October of the year before the year you ask about?
      `the Consumer Price Index for September` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Consumer Price Index for September, in the twelve months ending on 31 October of the year before the year you ask about?
      `the Consumer Price Index for October` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Consumer Price Index for October, in the twelve months ending on 31 October of the year before the year you ask about?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the Pension Index for a year` IS
    `s 43(1) — the Pension Index for a year before the exception`
        (LIST `the Consumer Price Index for November`, `the Consumer Price Index for December`, `the Consumer Price Index for January`, `the Consumer Price Index for February`, `the Consumer Price Index for March`, `the Consumer Price Index for April`, `the Consumer Price Index for May`, `the Consumer Price Index for June`, `the Consumer Price Index for July`, `the Consumer Price Index for August`, `the Consumer Price Index for September`, `the Consumer Price Index for October`)

-- s 43(2). The Pension Index never falls: if the calculation gives less than the index of the year before, that year's index is used.
@export What is the Pension Index for a year, given that it never falls (s 43(2))?
GIVEN `the Pension Index calculated for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What Pension Index does the calculation give for the year?
      `the Pension Index for the year before` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Pension Index for the year before?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the Pension Index for a year, given that it never falls` IS
    `s 43(2) — the Pension Index for a year` `the Pension Index calculated for the year` `the Pension Index for the year before`

§§ `Whether a benefit is payable to me (section 44)`

-- s 44(1)(a). A retirement pension is paid to a contributor who has reached 60. Reaching 60 is the first day of the month after the 60th birthday's month (s 2(2)).
-- Applying for it and the month it starts are other provisions (Division C, piece cp4).
@export Am I entitled to a retirement pension (s 44(1)(a))?
GIVEN `I am a contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a contributor under the Plan (see the question about being a contributor)?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date are you asking whether a retirement pension is payable to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a retirement pension` IF
    `s 44(1)(a) — a retirement pension is payable to a contributor who has reached sixty years of age` `I am a contributor` `my date of birth` `the date I am asking about`

-- s 44(2)(a). The minimum qualifying period for a disability pension: base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption in four of the last six calendar years in
-- the contributory period (or all of them, if fewer than six), or in 25 years of which three are in the last six, or, after an earlier disability benefit stopped, in each year since.
@export Have I made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a disability pension (s 44(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the number of my last six calendar years in my contributory period in which I made base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the last six calendar years included wholly or partly in your contributory period (or of all of them, if fewer than six), in how many did you make base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption?
      `the number of my calendar years in my contributory period in which I made base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of all the calendar years included wholly or partly in your contributory period did you make base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption?
      `I had an earlier disability benefit that stopped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have an earlier disability benefit that has stopped?
      `the number of my calendar years in my contributory period since the year that benefit stopped` IS A NUMBER @desc How many calendar years in your contributory period are the year that benefit stopped or later? (0 if none)
      `the number of those years in which I made base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of those years did you make base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a disability pension` IF
       `s 44(2)(a)(i) — at least four of the last six calendar years count, by number` `the number of my last six calendar years in my contributory period in which I made base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption`
    OR `s 44(2)(a)(i.1) — at least 25 calendar years count, three of them among the last six, by number` `the number of my calendar years in my contributory period in which I made base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption` `the number of my last six calendar years in my contributory period in which I made base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption`
    OR `s 44(2)(a)(ii) — every calendar year since the previous disability benefit ceased counts, by number` `I had an earlier disability benefit that stopped` `the number of my calendar years in my contributory period since the year that benefit stopped` `the number of those years in which I made base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption`

-- s 44(2.1). A late applicant's basic exemption for the year they would have been considered disabled: the Year's Basic Exemption times the months not excluded for disability, over 12,
-- if the year's base unadjusted pensionable earnings are less than the Year's Basic Exemption.
@export What is my basic exemption for the year I would have been considered disabled, if I applied late (s 44(2.1))?
GIVEN `the Year's Basic Exemption for that year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Year's Basic Exemption for that year, in dollars?
      `my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your base unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year, in dollars?
      `the number of months of that year that would not have been excluded by reason of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of that year would not have been excluded from your contributory period by reason of disability?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my basic exemption for the year I would have been considered disabled, if I applied late` IS
    `s 44(2.1) — the basic exemption for the year in which a late applicant would have been considered to have become disabled` `the Year's Basic Exemption for that year` `my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year` `the number of months of that year that would not have been excluded by reason of disability`

-- s 44(2.2). A late applicant who became disabled in a month in which they were a family allowance recipient, in the year the child turned seven and with base unadjusted
-- pensionable earnings below the basic exemption, is deemed to have the minimum qualifying period if a disability pension would have been payable had they become disabled a year earlier.
@export Am I deemed to have the minimum qualifying period as a late applicant who was a family allowance recipient (s 44(2.2))?
GIVEN `my application is a late application under subparagraph 44(1)(b)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application one to which subparagraph 44(1)(b)(ii) applies (a disability pension would have been payable had you applied earlier)?
      `I became disabled in a month in which I was a family allowance recipient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become disabled in a month in which you were a family allowance recipient?
      `in that year the child I received the allowance for reached seven` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the year you became disabled, did the child you received the family allowance for reach seven years of age?
      `my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year you became disabled, in dollars?
      `my basic exemption for that year without regard to subsection 20(2)` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your basic exemption for that year, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2), in dollars?
      `a disability pension would have been payable had I become disabled the year before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Without this subsection no disability pension is payable to you: would one have been payable to you under subparagraph 44(1)(b)(ii) had you become disabled in the year before?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed to have the minimum qualifying period as a late applicant who was a family allowance recipient` IF
    `s 44(2.2) — a late applicant is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` `my application is a late application under subparagraph 44(1)(b)(ii)` `I became disabled in a month in which I was a family allowance recipient` `in that year the child I received the allowance for reached seven` `my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year` `my basic exemption for that year without regard to subsection 20(2)` `a disability pension would have been payable had I become disabled the year before`

-- s 44(1)(b). A disability pension is paid to a contributor under 65, to whom no retirement pension is payable, who is disabled, and who (i) has the minimum qualifying period, or
-- (ii) or (iii) would have been paid a disability pension had the application been received earlier or a division not been made.
@export Am I entitled to a disability pension (s 44(1)(b))?
GIVEN `I am a contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a contributor under the Plan?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date are you asking whether a disability pension is payable to you?
      `a retirement pension is payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a retirement pension payable to you?
      `I am disabled under the Plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you considered disabled under the Plan (see the question about being disabled)?
      `I have made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a disability pension (see that question), or are you deemed to have by subsection 44(2.2)?
      `a disability pension would have been payable to me had my application been received earlier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a disability pension have been payable to you at the time you are deemed to have become disabled, had an application been received before your application was actually received?
      `a disability pension would have been payable to me had a division of my earnings not been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a disability pension have been payable to you at the time you are deemed to have become disabled, had a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1 not been made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a disability pension` IF
    `s 44(1)(b) — a disability pension is payable to a contributor who is disabled` `I am a contributor` `my date of birth` `the date I am asking about` `a retirement pension is payable to me` `I am disabled under the Plan` `I have made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period` `a disability pension would have been payable to me had my application been received earlier` `a disability pension would have been payable to me had a division of my earnings not been made`

-- s 44(3). The minimum qualifying period for a death benefit, a survivor's pension and an orphan's benefit: base contributions in at least a third of the years in the deceased
-- contributor's contributory period (not counting years after the year they turned 65 in which their earnings did not exceed the basic exemption), and at least three years; or ten years.
@export Did the deceased contributor make base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a death benefit, survivor's pension or orphan's benefit (s 44(3))?
GIVEN `the number of calendar years in the deceased contributor's contributory period, leaving out the years after the year they turned 65 in which their earnings did not exceed the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER @desc How many calendar years were included wholly or partly in the deceased contributor's contributory period, leaving out any year after the year they turned 65 in which their base unadjusted pensionable earnings were equal to or less than their basic exemption?
      `the number of those years in which a base contribution was made` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of those years was a base contribution made (their base unadjusted pensionable earnings exceeded the basic exemption)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the deceased contributor make base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a death benefit, survivor's pension or orphan's benefit` IF
       `s 44(3)(a) — base contributions were made for at least one third of the years, and for at least three years` `the number of those years in which a base contribution was made` `the number of calendar years in the deceased contributor's contributory period, leaving out the years after the year they turned 65 in which their earnings did not exceed the basic exemption`
    OR `s 44(3)(b) — base contributions were made for at least ten years` `the number of those years in which a base contribution was made`

-- s 44(1)(c). A death benefit is paid to the estate or succession of a deceased contributor who made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period.
@export Is a death benefit payable to the estate or succession of the deceased contributor (s 44(1)(c))?
GIVEN `the person has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person died?
      `the person was a contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person a contributor under the Plan?
      `the deceased contributor made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the deceased contributor make base contributions for the minimum qualifying period (see the question for a death benefit, survivor's pension or orphan's benefit)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a death benefit payable to the estate or succession of the deceased contributor` IF
    `s 44(1)(c) — a death benefit is payable to the estate or succession of a deceased contributor` `the person has died` `the person was a contributor` `the deceased contributor made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period`

-- s 44(1)(d). A survivor's pension: before 2019, to the survivor of a deceased contributor with the minimum qualifying period if the survivor has reached 65, or was then 35 or older, or had dependent children then, or is disabled; from 2019, to the survivor of such a contributor.
@export Am I entitled to a survivor's pension (s 44(1)(d))?
GIVEN `I am a survivor of the deceased contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a survivor of the deceased contributor under the Plan (see the question about being a survivor)?
      `the deceased contributor made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the deceased contributor make base contributions for the minimum qualifying period (see that question)?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date are you asking whether a survivor's pension is payable to you?
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the contributor die?
      `I was a survivor with dependent children when the contributor died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a survivor with dependent children when the contributor died?
      `I am disabled under the Plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disabled under the Plan?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a survivor's pension` IF
    `s 44(1)(d) — a survivor's pension is payable to the survivor of a deceased contributor` `I am a survivor of the deceased contributor` `the deceased contributor made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period` `my date of birth` `the date I am asking about` `the day the contributor died` `I was a survivor with dependent children when the contributor died` `I am disabled under the Plan`

-- s 44(1)(f). An orphan's benefit is paid to each orphan of a deceased contributor who made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period.
@export Am I entitled to an orphan's benefit (s 44(1)(f))?
GIVEN `I am an orphan of the deceased contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an orphan of the deceased contributor under the Plan (see that question)?
      `the deceased contributor made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the deceased contributor make base contributions for the minimum qualifying period (see that question)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to an orphan's benefit` IF
    `s 44(1)(f) — an orphan's benefit is payable to an orphan of a deceased contributor` `I am an orphan of the deceased contributor` `the deceased contributor made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period`

-- s 44(2), s 44(4). For a disabled contributor's child's benefit the minimum qualifying period is that of subsection (2) where the contributor is paid a disability pension, and that of subsection (4) where
-- the contributor is paid a post-retirement disability benefit.
@export Am I entitled to a disabled contributor's child's benefit (s 44(1)(e))?
GIVEN `I am a disabled contributor's child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a disabled contributor's child under the Plan (see that question)?
      `a disability pension is payable to the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a disability pension payable to the disabled contributor?
      `a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a post-retirement disability benefit payable to the disabled contributor?
      `the contributor has made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a disability pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contributor made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a disability pension (subsection 44(2))?
      `the contributor has made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a post-retirement disability benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contributor made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a post-retirement disability benefit (subsection 44(4))?
      `a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable to the contributor had an application been received earlier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit have been payable to the contributor at the time they are deemed to have become disabled, had an application been received before the application was actually received?
      `a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable to the contributor had a division not been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would one have been payable to the contributor at that time had a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1 not been made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a disabled contributor's child's benefit` IF
    `s 44(1)(e) — a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable to a child of a disabled contributor` `I am a disabled contributor's child` `a disability pension is payable to the contributor` `a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the contributor` `the contributor has made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a disability pension` `the contributor has made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a post-retirement disability benefit` `a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable to the contributor had an application been received earlier` `a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable to the contributor had a division not been made`

-- s 44(1)(g). A post-retirement benefit is paid to a beneficiary of a retirement pension under the Plan or a provincial plan who has made a contribution in respect of it.
@export Am I entitled to a post-retirement benefit (s 44(1)(g))?
GIVEN `I receive a retirement pension under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive a retirement pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan?
      `I have made a contribution in respect of the post-retirement benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a contribution in respect of the post-retirement benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a post-retirement benefit` IF
    `s 44(1)(g) — a post-retirement benefit is payable to a beneficiary of a retirement pension` `I receive a retirement pension under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` `I have made a contribution in respect of the post-retirement benefit`

-- s 44(4). The minimum qualifying period for a post-retirement disability benefit: base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption in four of the last six calendar years, or
-- in 25 years of which three are in the last six, or, after an earlier disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit stopped, in each year since.
@export Have I made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a post-retirement disability benefit (s 44(4))?
GIVEN `the number of my last six calendar years in my contributory period in which I made base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the last six calendar years included wholly or partly in your contributory period, in how many did you make base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption?
      `the number of my calendar years in my contributory period in which I made base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of all the calendar years included wholly or partly in your contributory period did you make base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption?
      `I had an earlier disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit that stopped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have an earlier disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit that has stopped?
      `the number of my calendar years in my contributory period since the year that benefit stopped` IS A NUMBER @desc How many calendar years in your contributory period are the year that benefit stopped or later? (0 if none)
      `the number of those years in which I made base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of those years did you make base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a post-retirement disability benefit` IF
       `s 44(4)(a) — at least four of the last six calendar years count, by number` `the number of my last six calendar years in my contributory period in which I made base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption`
    OR `s 44(4)(b) — at least 25 calendar years count, three of them among the last six, by number` `the number of my calendar years in my contributory period in which I made base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption` `the number of my last six calendar years in my contributory period in which I made base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption`
    OR `s 44(4)(c) — every calendar year since the previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit ceased counts, by number` `I had an earlier disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit that stopped` `the number of my calendar years in my contributory period since the year that benefit stopped` `the number of those years in which I made base contributions on earnings of at least the basic exemption`

-- s 44(1)(h). A post-retirement disability benefit is paid to a beneficiary of a retirement pension who is under 65 and disabled and who has the minimum qualifying period, with the period ending after 2018, or who would have been paid one had the application been received earlier or a division not been made.
@export Am I entitled to a post-retirement disability benefit (s 44(1)(h))?
GIVEN `I receive a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive a retirement pension?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date are you asking whether a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to you?
      `I am disabled under the Plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disabled under the Plan?
      `I have made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a post-retirement disability benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a post-retirement disability benefit (see that question)?
      `the month in which I am determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph 44(1)(h)` IS A DATE @desc In which month were you determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph 44(1)(h)? (Any date in that month.)
      `a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable to me had my application been received earlier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a post-retirement disability benefit have been payable to you at the time you are deemed to have become disabled, had an application been received before your application was actually received?
      `a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable to me had a division of my earnings not been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a post-retirement disability benefit have been payable to you at that time had a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1 not been made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a post-retirement disability benefit` IF
    `s 44(1)(h) — a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to a beneficiary of a retirement pension who is disabled` `I receive a retirement pension` `my date of birth` `the date I am asking about` `I am disabled under the Plan` `I have made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period for a post-retirement disability benefit` `the month in which I am determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph 44(1)(h)` `a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable to me had my application been received earlier` `a post-retirement disability benefit would have been payable to me had a division of my earnings not been made`

§§ `Conviction for killing the contributor, and survivor's pension after a division (sections 44.1 and 44.2)`

-- s 44.1(3), (6), (7), (8). Whether a conviction engages section 44.1: first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor, or a conviction outside Canada the Minister deems to be one; not manslaughter with release on a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code.
@export Is my conviction one that engages section 44.1 (s 44.1)?
GIVEN `I have been convicted of first or second degree murder of the contributor, murder within the meaning of section 231 of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of first or second degree murder of the contributor (murder within the meaning of section 231 of the Criminal Code)?
      `I have been convicted of manslaughter of the contributor, manslaughter within the meaning of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of manslaughter of the contributor (manslaughter within the meaning of the Criminal Code)?
      `I have been convicted by a court outside Canada of an offence that, if committed in Canada, would have constituted first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted by a court outside Canada of an offence that, if committed in Canada, would have constituted first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor?
      `the Minister deems the conviction outside Canada to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister deemed that conviction outside Canada to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter?
      `I am released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, on a conviction of manslaughter, released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my conviction one that engages section 44.1` IF
    `s 44.1 — a conviction that engages this section` `I have been convicted of first or second degree murder of the contributor, murder within the meaning of section 231 of the Criminal Code` `I have been convicted of manslaughter of the contributor, manslaughter within the meaning of the Criminal Code` `I have been convicted by a court outside Canada of an offence that, if committed in Canada, would have constituted first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` `the Minister deems the conviction outside Canada to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter` `I am released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code`

-- s 44.1(1)(a). A survivor's pension is not payable to someone the Minister is informed and satisfied has been convicted of killing the contributor.
@export Is a survivor's pension not payable to me because of a conviction for killing the contributor (s 44.1(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the Minister is informed and satisfied that I have been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister informed and satisfied that you have been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor?
      `my conviction engages section 44.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your conviction engage section 44.1 (see that question)?
      `my entitlement has been reinstated under subsection 44.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your entitlement been reinstated under subsection 44.1(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a survivor's pension not payable to me because of a conviction for killing the contributor` IF
    `s 44.1(1)(a) — a survivor's pension is not payable to an individual convicted of killing the contributor` `the Minister is informed and satisfied that I have been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` `my conviction engages section 44.1` `my entitlement has been reinstated under subsection 44.1(2)`

-- s 44.1(1)(b). A death benefit is not payable to such a person either.
@export Is a death benefit not payable to me because of a conviction for killing the contributor (s 44.1(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the Minister is informed and satisfied that I have been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister informed and satisfied that you have been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor?
      `my conviction engages section 44.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your conviction engage section 44.1 (see that question)?
      `my entitlement has been reinstated under subsection 44.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your entitlement been reinstated under subsection 44.1(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a death benefit not payable to me because of a conviction for killing the contributor` IF
    `s 44.1(1)(b) — a death benefit is not payable to an individual convicted of killing the contributor` `the Minister is informed and satisfied that I have been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` `my conviction engages section 44.1` `my entitlement has been reinstated under subsection 44.1(2)`

-- s 44.1(1)(c). An orphan's benefit is not payable to such a person who has received an adult sentence and is 18 or older.
@export Is an orphan's benefit not payable to me because of a conviction for killing the contributor (s 44.1(1)(c))?
GIVEN `the Minister is informed and satisfied that I have been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister informed and satisfied that you have been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor?
      `my conviction engages section 44.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your conviction engage section 44.1 (see that question)?
      `the Minister is informed and satisfied that I have received an adult sentence for that murder or manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister informed and satisfied that you have received an adult sentence for that murder or manslaughter?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date are you asking whether the orphan's benefit is payable?
      `my entitlement has been reinstated under subsection 44.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your entitlement been reinstated under subsection 44.1(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an orphan's benefit not payable to me because of a conviction for killing the contributor` IF
    `s 44.1(1)(c) — an orphan's benefit is not payable to an individual convicted of killing the contributor` `the Minister is informed and satisfied that I have been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the contributor` `my conviction engages section 44.1` `the Minister is informed and satisfied that I have received an adult sentence for that murder or manslaughter` `my date of birth` `the date I am asking about` `my entitlement has been reinstated under subsection 44.1(2)`

-- s 44.1(2). The Minister reinstates entitlement, and repays what was recovered, when informed and satisfied that the conviction was reversed, the charges withdrawn or the proceedings stayed, and that every right of appeal has been exhausted.
@export Will my entitlement be reinstated and what was recovered repaid (s 44.1(2))?
GIVEN `the Minister is informed and satisfied that my conviction has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn, or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister informed and satisfied that your conviction has been reversed, the charges withdrawn, or the proceedings stayed and not recommenced within the required time period?
      `the Minister is informed and satisfied that all rights of appeal have been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister informed and satisfied that all rights of appeal have been exhausted?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my entitlement be reinstated and what was recovered repaid` IF
    `s 44.1(2) — the individual's entitlement is reinstated and any amount recovered is repaid` `the Minister is informed and satisfied that my conviction has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn, or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time period` `the Minister is informed and satisfied that all rights of appeal have been exhausted`

-- s 44.1(4). The paired liability: what I received, including before the conviction, is a debt due to Her Majesty if a bar applies.
@export What am I liable to repay because of a conviction for killing the contributor (s 44.1(4))?
GIVEN `I have received a survivor's pension, death benefit or orphan's benefit referred to in section 44.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received a survivor's pension, a death benefit or an orphan's benefit referred to in section 44.1?
      `a bar of subsection 44.1(1) applies to me on what the Minister is now informed and satisfied of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a bar of subsection 44.1(1) apply to you on what the Minister is now informed and satisfied of?
      `the total of the amounts I received, including any paid before the date of the conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the amounts you received, including any paid before the date of the conviction, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What am I liable to repay because of a conviction for killing the contributor` IS
    `s 44.1(4) — the amount received that is a debt due to Her Majesty` `I have received a survivor's pension, death benefit or orphan's benefit referred to in section 44.1` `a bar of subsection 44.1(1) applies to me on what the Minister is now informed and satisfied of` (LIST `the total of the amounts I received, including any paid before the date of the conviction`)

-- s 44.2. A survivor's pension is not payable if, on or after 1 January 2025, a division took place under paragraph 55.1(1)(b) between the contributor and me, unless at the death I had been cohabiting with the contributor in a new conjugal relationship for a continuous year.
@export Is a survivor's pension not payable to me because of an earlier division of earnings (s 44.2)?
GIVEN `a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings has taken place under paragraph 55.1(1)(b) between the contributor and me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings taken place under paragraph 55.1(1)(b) between the contributor and you?
      `the day on which that division took place` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that division take place? (Any date if none did.)
      `at the contributor's death I had been cohabiting with the contributor in a new conjugal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the contributor's death, had you been cohabiting with the contributor in a new conjugal relationship?
      `the day on which that cohabitation began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that new cohabitation begin? (Any date if there was none.)
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the contributor die?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a survivor's pension not payable to me because of an earlier division of earnings` IF
    `s 44.2 — a survivor's pension is not payable to an individual after a division of earnings` `a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings has taken place under paragraph 55.1(1)(b) between the contributor and me` `the day on which that division took place` `at the contributor's death I had been cohabiting with the contributor in a new conjugal relationship` `the day on which that cohabitation began` `the day the contributor died`

§§ `My retirement pension and its adjustments (sections 45 and 46)`

-- s 46(1). The basic monthly amount of a retirement pension: 25 per cent of average monthly pensionable earnings, plus 8.33 per cent of the first additional monthly
-- pensionable earnings, plus 33.33 per cent of the second additional monthly pensionable earnings.
@export What is the basic monthly amount of my retirement pension (s 46(1))?
GIVEN `my average monthly pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your average monthly pensionable earnings, in dollars (see the question about average monthly pensionable earnings)?
      `my first additional monthly pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your first additional monthly pensionable earnings, in dollars? (0 if none)
      `my second additional monthly pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your second additional monthly pensionable earnings, in dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the basic monthly amount of my retirement pension` IS
    `s 46(1) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension` `my average monthly pensionable earnings` `my first additional monthly pensionable earnings` `my second additional monthly pensionable earnings`

-- s 46(2). A former disability pension recipient whose retirement pension a division of earnings reduces has the first portion computed on the earnings as they were before the division,
-- in proportion to the months excluded for disability.
@export What is the first portion of my retirement pension as a former disability pension recipient whose pension a division reduces (s 46(2))?
GIVEN `I am a former disability pension recipient and a division under section 55 or 55.1 is approved before or after my retirement pension starts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a former disability pension recipient in respect of whom a division under section 55 or 55.1 is approved, before or after your retirement pension starts?
      `the division reduces the retirement pension otherwise payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the division reduce the retirement pension that would otherwise be payable to you?
      `the portion of my retirement pension that would be payable had my base unadjusted pensionable earnings not been divided` IS A NUMBER @desc What would the portion under paragraph 46(1)(a) be, had your base unadjusted pensionable earnings not been subject to the division, in dollars?
      `the portion of my retirement pension that would be payable following the division` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the portion under paragraph 46(1)(a) following the division, in dollars?
      `the number of months excluded from my contributory period by reason of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are excluded from your contributory period by reason of disability?
      `the number of months in my contributory period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in your contributory period calculated under section 49?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the first portion of my retirement pension as a former disability pension recipient whose pension a division reduces` IS
    `s 46(2) — the portion of a retirement pension under paragraph (1)(a) for a former disability pension recipient whose pension a division reduces` `I am a former disability pension recipient and a division under section 55 or 55.1 is approved before or after my retirement pension starts` `the division reduces the retirement pension otherwise payable to me` `the portion of my retirement pension that would be payable had my base unadjusted pensionable earnings not been divided` `the portion of my retirement pension that would be payable following the division` `the number of months excluded from my contributory period by reason of disability` `the number of months in my contributory period`

-- s 46(3). A retirement pension that becomes payable after 1986 and before 2011 is the basic monthly amount adjusted by the Minister's factor for the time between its start and the month I reach 65 (at most five years).
@export What is my retirement pension if it starts after 1986 and before 2011, adjusted for starting early or late (s 46(3))?
GIVEN `the basic monthly amount of my retirement pension under subsection 46(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic monthly amount of your retirement pension under subsection 46(1) or (2), in dollars?
      `the month with which my retirement pension commences` IS A DATE @desc In which month does your retirement pension start? (Any date in that month.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the factor fixed by the Minister for the time interval` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the factor the Minister has fixed, on the advice of the Chief Actuary, for the time between the start of your pension and the month you reach 65? (The Act leaves the figure to the Minister; the Regulations may give it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my retirement pension if it starts after 1986 and before 2011, adjusted for starting early or late` IS
    `s 46(3) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 1986 and before 2011, adjusted by the Minister's factor` `the basic monthly amount of my retirement pension under subsection 46(1) or (2)` `the month with which my retirement pension commences` `my date of birth` `the factor fixed by the Minister for the time interval`

-- s 46(3.1). A retirement pension that becomes payable after 2010 is adjusted by the factor fixed under subsection (7) (the Regulations set it: reg 78.3, 78.4).
@export What is my retirement pension if it starts after 2010, adjusted for starting early or late (s 46(3.1))?
GIVEN `the basic monthly amount of my retirement pension under subsection 46(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic monthly amount of your retirement pension under subsection 46(1) or (2), in dollars?
      `the month with which my retirement pension commences` IS A DATE @desc In which month does your retirement pension start? (Any date in that month.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the adjustment factor fixed under subsection 46(7)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the adjustment factor fixed under subsection 46(7) for the time between the start of your pension and the month you reach 65?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my retirement pension if it starts after 2010, adjusted for starting early or late` IS
    `s 46(3.1) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 2010, adjusted by the factor fixed under subsection (7)` `the basic monthly amount of my retirement pension under subsection 46(1) or (2)` `the month with which my retirement pension commences` `my date of birth` `the adjustment factor fixed under subsection 46(7)`

-- s 46(4). The factor applied after a division increases a retirement pension.
@export What adjustment factor applies after a division increases my retirement pension (s 46(4))?
GIVEN `the adjustment factor when my retirement pension first became payable` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the adjustment factor when your retirement pension first became payable?
      `the basic monthly amount before the division` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the basic monthly amount of your retirement pension before the division, in dollars?
      `the adjustment factor had my retirement pension commenced in the month the increase commences to be payable` IS A NUMBER @desc What would the adjustment factor have been had your retirement pension commenced in the month in which the increase starts to be paid?
      `the basic monthly amount immediately following the division` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic monthly amount immediately following the division, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What adjustment factor applies after a division increases my retirement pension` IS
    `s 46(4) — the adjustment factor applied after a division increases a retirement pension` `the adjustment factor when my retirement pension first became payable` `the basic monthly amount before the division` `the adjustment factor had my retirement pension commenced in the month the increase commences to be payable` `the basic monthly amount immediately following the division`

-- s 46(5). When I get both a retirement pension and a survivor's pension that is reduced from its full amount, the adjustment factor is applied only to what is left after the survivor's pension reduction.
@export What is my retirement pension when my survivor's pension has been reduced (s 46(5))?
GIVEN `an agreement under section 80 provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an agreement under section 80 (with a province or another country's plan) provide otherwise?
      `I receive both a retirement pension and a survivor's pension, and the survivor's pension is reduced from its full amount under subsection 58(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive both a retirement pension and a survivor's pension, with the survivor's pension reduced from its full amount under subsection 58(2)?
      `the basic monthly amount of my retirement pension under subsection 46(1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic monthly amount of your retirement pension under subsection 46(1) or (2), in dollars?
      `the downward adjustment factor resulting from subsection 46(3), (3.1) or (4)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the downward adjustment factor resulting from subsection 46(3), (3.1) or (4)?
      `the amount by which my survivor's pension has been reduced` IS A NUMBER @desc By how much has your survivor's pension been reduced, in dollars a month?
      `the Pension Index for the year my retirement pension first commenced to be payable` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Pension Index for the year in which your retirement pension first commenced to be payable?
      `the Pension Index for the year in which my survivor's pension is reduced` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the year in which your survivor's pension is reduced?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my retirement pension when my survivor's pension has been reduced` IS
    `s 46(5) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension when the factor is applied only to the amount left after a survivor's pension reduction` `an agreement under section 80 provides otherwise` `I receive both a retirement pension and a survivor's pension, and the survivor's pension is reduced from its full amount under subsection 58(2)` `the basic monthly amount of my retirement pension under subsection 46(1) or (2)` `the downward adjustment factor resulting from subsection 46(3), (3.1) or (4)` `the amount by which my survivor's pension has been reduced` `the Pension Index for the year my retirement pension first commenced to be payable` `the Pension Index for the year in which my survivor's pension is reduced`

-- s 46(6). For an increase due to a division after 65, the time interval on which the upward factor is based.
@export Over what time interval is the upward adjustment for a division after I reach 65 worked out (s 46(6))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings takes place` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings take place?
      `the month with which my retirement pension commences` IS A DATE @desc In which month does your retirement pension commence? (Any date in that month.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Over what time interval is the upward adjustment for a division after I reach 65 worked out` IS
    `s 46(6) — the time interval, in months, on which the upward adjustment factor for an increase due to a division after age 65 is based` `my date of birth` `the day the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings takes place` `the month with which my retirement pension commences`

-- s 45(2). Each year a benefit is adjusted by the Pension Index: the amount for a month in the following year is the amount that would have been payable, times the Pension Index of the following year over that of the year before it.
@export What will be paid to me for a month in the following year after the annual adjustment (s 45(2))?
GIVEN `the amount that would have been payable for the month if no adjustment had been made for the following year` IS A NUMBER @desc What would have been payable for the month if no adjustment had been made for the following year, in dollars?
      `the Pension Index for the following year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the following year?
      `the Pension Index for the year preceding the following year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Pension Index for the year before the following year?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What will be paid to me for a month in the following year after the annual adjustment` IS
    `s 45(2) — the amount payable for a month in the following year after the annual adjustment` `the amount that would have been payable for the month if no adjustment had been made for the following year` `the Pension Index for the following year` `the Pension Index for the year preceding the following year`

§§ `My average monthly pensionable earnings and my contributory period (sections 47 to 50.2)`

-- s 48(1). Average monthly pensionable earnings before the deductions of subsections (2) to (4): total pensionable earnings over the months in the contributory period, taken over at least the basic number of contributory months.
@export What are my average monthly pensionable earnings before any deduction (s 48(1))?
GIVEN `the month with which my retirement pension commences` IS A DATE @desc In which month does your retirement pension commence? (Any date in that month.)
      `my total pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total pensionable earnings over your contributory period, in dollars (section 50)?
      `the total number of months in my contributory period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months are in your contributory period (see the question about the months in a contributory period)?
      `my basic number of contributory months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic number of contributory months (see that question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my average monthly pensionable earnings before any deduction` IS
    `s 48(1) — the average monthly pensionable earnings before the deductions` `the month with which my retirement pension commences` `my total pensionable earnings` `the total number of months in my contributory period` `my basic number of contributory months`

-- s 48(4)(a)(i). The percentage of the months remaining that is deducted.
@export What percentage of my remaining months is deducted when working out my average (s 48(4)(a)(i))?
GIVEN `the month with which my retirement pension or other benefit becomes payable` IS A DATE @desc In which month does your retirement pension or other benefit become payable? (Any date in that month.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What percentage of my remaining months is deducted when working out my average` IS
    `s 48(4)(a)(i) — the percentage of the months remaining that is deducted` `the month with which my retirement pension or other benefit becomes payable`

-- s 48.1. First additional monthly pensionable earnings: total first additional earnings over 480 months where the first additional contributory period is not longer.
@export What are my first additional monthly pensionable earnings when my first additional contributory period is no longer than 480 months (s 48.1(a))?
GIVEN `my total first additional pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total first additional pensionable earnings, in dollars (section 50.1)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my first additional monthly pensionable earnings when my first additional contributory period is no longer than 480 months` IS
    `s 48.1(a) — the first additional monthly pensionable earnings when the first additional contributory period is not more than 480 months` `my total first additional pensionable earnings`

-- s 48.2. The same for second additional earnings.
@export What are my second additional monthly pensionable earnings when my second additional contributory period is no longer than 480 months (s 48.2(a))?
GIVEN `my total second additional pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total second additional pensionable earnings, in dollars (section 50.2)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my second additional monthly pensionable earnings when my second additional contributory period is no longer than 480 months` IS
    `s 48.2(a) — the second additional monthly pensionable earnings when the second additional contributory period is not more than 480 months` `my total second additional pensionable earnings`

-- s 49. The contributory period begins at the later of 1 January 1966 and the month in which the contributor reaches 18.
@export In which month does my contributory period begin (s 49)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `In which month does my contributory period begin` IS
    `s 49 — the first month of the contributory period` `my date of birth`

-- s 49. The last month of the contributory period for a retirement pension.
@export In which month does my contributory period end for a retirement pension (s 49)?
GIVEN `the month with which my retirement pension commences` IS A DATE @desc In which month does your retirement pension commence? (Any date in that month.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I made a contribution for earnings after I reached 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a contribution for earnings after you reached 65?
      `the month for which I last made a contribution for earnings after reaching 65` IS A DATE @desc For which month did you last make a contribution for earnings after reaching 65? (Any date if you did not.)
      `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contributor died?
      `the month in which I died` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the contributor die? (Any date if they have not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `In which month does my contributory period end for a retirement pension` IS
    `s 49 — the last month of the contributory period for a benefit` `a retirement pension` `the month with which my retirement pension commences` `my date of birth`
        (IF `I made a contribution for earnings after I reached 65` THEN JUST `the month for which I last made a contribution for earnings after reaching 65` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `I have died` THEN JUST `the month in which I died` ELSE NOTHING)
        (JUST `the month with which my retirement pension commences`)

-- s 49. The number of months in the contributory period: from the first month to the last, leaving out the months excluded for disability or for family allowance recipients.
@export How many months are in my contributory period (s 49)?
GIVEN `the first month of my contributory period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first month of your contributory period? (Any date in that month.)
      `the last month of my contributory period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last month of your contributory period? (Any date in that month.)
      `the number of months from the first to the last that are excluded by reason of disability or as a family allowance recipient` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months from the first to the last are excluded from your contributory period under paragraph 49(c) or (d)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months are in my contributory period` IS
    `s 49 — the number of months in the contributory period` `the first month of my contributory period` `the last month of my contributory period` `the number of months from the first to the last that are excluded by reason of disability or as a family allowance recipient`

-- s 49(c), (d). A month is excluded from the contributory period if it was excluded by reason of disability, or, for a benefit payable for a month after December 1977, I was a family allowance recipient for the month in a year in which my base unadjusted pensionable earnings were at or under my basic exemption.
@export Is a month excluded from my contributory period (s 49(c), (d))?
GIVEN `the month was excluded from my contributory period under the Plan or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the month excluded from your contributory period under the Plan or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability?
      `the month for which the benefit is payable` IS A DATE @desc For which month is the benefit payable? (Any date in that month.)
      `I was a family allowance recipient for the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a family allowance recipient for the month?
      `my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year of the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year of the month, in dollars?
      `my basic exemption for the year of the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your basic exemption for the year of the month, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a month excluded from my contributory period` IF
    `s 49(c), (d) — a month is excluded from the contributory period` `the month was excluded from my contributory period under the Plan or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` `the month for which the benefit is payable` `I was a family allowance recipient for the month` `my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year of the month` `my basic exemption for the year of the month`

-- s 49.1. The first additional contributory period begins at the later of 1 January 2019 and the month in which I reach 18, and ends as the section says.
@export In which month does my first additional contributory period begin (s 49.1)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `In which month does my first additional contributory period begin` IS
    `s 49.1 — the first month of the first additional contributory period` `my date of birth`

@export In which month does my first additional contributory period end (s 49.1)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contributor died?
      `the month in which I died` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the contributor die? (Any date if they have not.)
      `my retirement pension has commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a retirement pension commenced?
      `the month with which my retirement pension commences` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the retirement pension commence? (Any date if it has not.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `In which month does my first additional contributory period end` IS
    `s 49.1 — the last month of the first additional contributory period` `my date of birth`
        (IF `I have died` THEN JUST `the month in which I died` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `my retirement pension has commenced` THEN JUST `the month with which my retirement pension commences` ELSE NOTHING)

@export In which month does my second additional contributory period begin (s 49.2)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `In which month does my second additional contributory period begin` IS
    `s 49.2 — the first month of the second additional contributory period` `my date of birth`

@export In which month does my second additional contributory period end (s 49.2)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contributor died?
      `the month in which I died` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the contributor die? (Any date if they have not.)
      `my retirement pension has commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a retirement pension commenced?
      `the month with which my retirement pension commences` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the retirement pension commence? (Any date if it has not.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `In which month does my second additional contributory period end` IS
    `s 49.2 — the last month of the second additional contributory period` `my date of birth`
        (IF `I have died` THEN JUST `the month in which I died` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `my retirement pension has commenced` THEN JUST `the month with which my retirement pension commences` ELSE NOTHING)

§§ `My unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year (sections 53 to 54.2)`

-- s 53(1). The base unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year: the larger of the contributory salary and wages and self-employed earnings and the earnings on which base contributions were made,
-- but nothing if the first amount does not exceed the basic exemption, and capped as the paragraphs say.
@export What are my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year (s 53(1))?
GIVEN `my contributory salary and wages for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your contributory salary and wages for the year, in dollars?
      `I am an individual described in section 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an individual described in section 10 (a self-employed person who is to contribute)?
      `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your contributory self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars?
      `my salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your salary and wages on which a base contribution was made for the year, in dollars?
      `the base contribution I was required to make for the year on my self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What base contribution were you required to make for the year on your self-employed earnings, in dollars?
      `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be my salary and wages on which a base contribution was made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount is determined, in the prescribed manner, to be your salary and wages on which a base contribution was made for the year under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `the base contribution I was required to make for the year under a provincial pension plan on my self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What base contribution were you required to make for the year under a provincial pension plan on your self-employed earnings, in dollars?
      `the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year, as a decimal (for example 0.119)?
      `my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year, in dollars?
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year` IS
    `s 53(1) — the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year` `my contributory salary and wages for the year` `I am an individual described in section 10` `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` `my salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year` `the base contribution I was required to make for the year on my self-employed earnings` `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be my salary and wages on which a base contribution was made for the year under a provincial pension plan` `the base contribution I was required to make for the year under a provincial pension plan on my self-employed earnings` `the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` `my basic exemption for the year` `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year`

-- s 53(2)(a). In the year a retirement pension becomes payable, the basic exemption is the Year's Basic Exemption prorated over the months not excluded and before the pension starts.
@export What is my basic exemption in the year my retirement pension becomes payable (s 53(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the Year's Basic Exemption` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Year's Basic Exemption for that year, in dollars?
      `the number of months in the year that are not excluded from my contributory period and are before my retirement pension becomes payable` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in that year are not excluded from your contributory period and are before your retirement pension becomes payable?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my basic exemption in the year my retirement pension becomes payable` IS
    `s 53(2)(a) — the contributor's basic exemption for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable` `the Year's Basic Exemption` `the number of months in the year that are not excluded from my contributory period and are before my retirement pension becomes payable`

-- s 53(2)(b). The same for my maximum pensionable earnings.
@export What are my maximum pensionable earnings in the year my retirement pension becomes payable (s 53(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year, in dollars?
      `the number of months in the year that are not excluded from my contributory period and are before my retirement pension becomes payable` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in that year are not excluded from your contributory period and are before your retirement pension becomes payable?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my maximum pensionable earnings in the year my retirement pension becomes payable` IS
    `s 53(2)(b) — the contributor's maximum pensionable earnings for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the number of months in the year that are not excluded from my contributory period and are before my retirement pension becomes payable`

-- s 53.1(1). The first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year.
@export What are my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year (s 53.1(1))?
GIVEN `my contributory salary and wages for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your contributory salary and wages for the year, in dollars?
      `I am an individual described in section 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an individual described in section 10?
      `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your contributory self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars?
      `my salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your salary and wages on which a first additional contribution was made for the year, in dollars?
      `the first additional contribution I was required to make for the year on my self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What first additional contribution were you required to make for the year on your self-employed earnings, in dollars?
      `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be my salary and wages on which a first additional contribution was made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount is determined, in the prescribed manner, to be your salary and wages on which a first additional contribution was made for the year under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `the first additional contribution I was required to make for the year under a provincial pension plan on my self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What first additional contribution were you required to make for the year under a provincial pension plan on your self-employed earnings, in dollars?
      `the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year, as a decimal?
      `my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year, in dollars?
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year` IS
    `s 53.1(1) — the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year` `my contributory salary and wages for the year` `I am an individual described in section 10` `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` `my salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` `the first additional contribution I was required to make for the year on my self-employed earnings` `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be my salary and wages on which a first additional contribution was made for the year under a provincial pension plan` `the first additional contribution I was required to make for the year under a provincial pension plan on my self-employed earnings` `the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` `my basic exemption for the year` `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year`

-- s 53.2(1). The second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year.
@export What are my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year (s 53.2(1))?
GIVEN `my contributory salary and wages for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your contributory salary and wages for the year, in dollars?
      `I am an individual described in section 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an individual described in section 10?
      `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your contributory self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars?
      `my salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your salary and wages on which a second additional contribution was made for the year, in dollars?
      `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be my salary and wages on which a second additional contribution was made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount is determined, in the prescribed manner, to be your salary and wages on which a second additional contribution was made for the year under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `the second additional contribution I was required to make for the year under a provincial pension plan on my self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What second additional contribution were you required to make for the year under a provincial pension plan on your self-employed earnings, in dollars?
      `the second additional contribution I was required to make for the year on my self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What second additional contribution were you required to make for the year on your self-employed earnings, in dollars?
      `the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year, as a decimal?
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars?
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year` IS
    `s 53.2(1) — the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year` `my contributory salary and wages for the year` `I am an individual described in section 10` `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` `my salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year` `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be my salary and wages on which a second additional contribution was made for the year under a provincial pension plan` `the second additional contribution I was required to make for the year under a provincial pension plan on my self-employed earnings` `the second additional contribution I was required to make for the year on my self-employed earnings` `the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`

-- s 53.5, 53.6. A year in which a family allowance recipient has an amount attributed: the amount determined for the year, or the attributed amount if it is larger (the sections say which).
@export What are my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year in which an amount is attributed to me as a family allowance recipient (s 53.5)?
GIVEN `my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings determined under section 53.1 for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year under section 53.1, in dollars?
      `an amount is attributed to me under section 53.3 for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an amount attributed to you for the year under section 53.3 (you were a family allowance recipient)?
      `the amount attributed to me under section 53.3 for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount is attributed to you under section 53.3 for the year, in dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year in which an amount is attributed to me as a family allowance recipient` IS
    `s 53.5 — the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of attribution` `my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings determined under section 53.1 for the year` (IF `an amount is attributed to me under section 53.3 for the year` THEN JUST `the amount attributed to me under section 53.3 for the year` ELSE NOTHING)

@export What are my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year in which an amount is attributed to me as a family allowance recipient (s 53.6)?
GIVEN `my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings determined under section 53.2 for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year under section 53.2, in dollars?
      `an amount is attributed to me under section 53.4 for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an amount attributed to you for the year under section 53.4 (you were a family allowance recipient)?
      `the amount attributed to me under section 53.4 for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount is attributed to you under section 53.4 for the year, in dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year in which an amount is attributed to me as a family allowance recipient` IS
    `s 53.6 — the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of attribution` `my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings determined under section 53.2 for the year` (IF `an amount is attributed to me under section 53.4 for the year` THEN JUST `the amount attributed to me under section 53.4 for the year` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 54, 54.1, 54.2. A year in which a division is made: the earnings of section 53, 53.1 or 53.2 are adjusted for a division under the Act and under a provincial plan.
@export What are my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year in which my earnings are divided (s 54)?
GIVEN `my base unadjusted pensionable earnings determined under section 53 for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year under section 53, in dollars?
      `a division under section 55 or 55.1 attributed base unadjusted pensionable earnings to me for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a division under section 55 or 55.1 attribute base unadjusted pensionable earnings to you for the year?
      `the base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me for the year by a division under section 55 or 55.1` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was attributed to you for the year by the division under section 55 or 55.1, in dollars? (0 if none)
      `a division under a provincial pension plan attributed base unadjusted pensionable earnings to me for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a division under a provincial pension plan attribute base unadjusted pensionable earnings to you for the year?
      `the base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me for the year by a division under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was attributed to you for the year by the division under the provincial pension plan, in dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year in which my earnings are divided` IS
    `s 54 — the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` `my base unadjusted pensionable earnings determined under section 53 for the year`
        (IF `a division under section 55 or 55.1 attributed base unadjusted pensionable earnings to me for the year` THEN JUST `the base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me for the year by a division under section 55 or 55.1` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `a division under a provincial pension plan attributed base unadjusted pensionable earnings to me for the year` THEN JUST `the base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me for the year by a division under a provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING)

@export What are my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year in which my earnings are divided (s 54.1)?
GIVEN `my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings determined under section 53.1 for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year under section 53.1, in dollars?
      `a division under section 55.1 attributed first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings to me for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a division under section 55.1 attribute first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings to you for the year?
      `the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me for the year by a division under section 55.1` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was attributed to you for the year by the division under section 55.1, in dollars? (0 if none)
      `a division under a provincial pension plan attributed first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings to me for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a division under a provincial pension plan attribute first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings to you for the year?
      `the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me for the year by a division under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was attributed to you for the year by the division under the provincial pension plan, in dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year in which my earnings are divided` IS
    `s 54.1 — the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` `my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings determined under section 53.1 for the year`
        (IF `a division under section 55.1 attributed first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings to me for the year` THEN JUST `the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me for the year by a division under section 55.1` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `a division under a provincial pension plan attributed first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings to me for the year` THEN JUST `the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me for the year by a division under a provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING)

@export What are my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year in which my earnings are divided (s 54.2)?
GIVEN `my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings determined under section 53.2 for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year under section 53.2, in dollars?
      `a division under section 55.1 attributed second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings to me for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a division under section 55.1 attribute second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings to you for the year?
      `the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me for the year by a division under section 55.1` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was attributed to you for the year by the division under section 55.1, in dollars? (0 if none)
      `a division under a provincial pension plan attributed second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings to me for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a division under a provincial pension plan attribute second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings to you for the year?
      `the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me for the year by a division under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was attributed to you for the year by the division under the provincial pension plan, in dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year in which my earnings are divided` IS
    `s 54.2 — the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` `my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings determined under section 53.2 for the year`
        (IF `a division under section 55.1 attributed second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings to me for the year` THEN JUST `the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me for the year by a division under section 55.1` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `a division under a provincial pension plan attributed second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings to me for the year` THEN JUST `the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me for the year by a division under a provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING)

§§ `Dividing earnings with a former spouse or partner: judgments between 1978 and 1987 (section 55)`

-- s 55(1). A former spouse (or their estate, or someone on their behalf) may apply in writing for a division of earnings within 36 months after a divorce or nullity judgment given from 1 January 1978 up to 1 January 1987, or at any time if both agree in writing.
@export May I apply for a division of earnings after a divorce or annulment between 1978 and 1987 (s 55(1))?
GIVEN `the application is made in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made in writing to the Minister?
      `the application is made by or on behalf of either former spouse, by the estate or succession of either, or by a person who may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made by or on behalf of either former spouse, by the estate or succession of either, or by a person who may be prescribed?
      `the day of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the judgment granting the divorce, or the judgment of nullity of the marriage, rendered?
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is (or was) the application made?
      `both former spouses agree in writing that the application may be made at any time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do both former spouses agree in writing that the application may be made at any time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply for a division of earnings after a divorce or annulment between 1978 and 1987` IF
    `s 55(1) — an application for a division of the unadjusted pensionable earnings of former spouses may be made` `the application is made in writing to the Minister` `the application is made by or on behalf of either former spouse, by the estate or succession of either, or by a person who may be prescribed` `the day of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage` `the day the application is made` `both former spouses agree in writing that the application may be made at any time`

-- s 55(2)(a). The Minister may approve the application only if the former spouses cohabited for at least 36 consecutive months during the marriage.
@export Did we cohabit long enough for a division after a divorce or annulment between 1978 and 1987 (s 55(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the number of consecutive months during the marriage that we cohabited` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many consecutive months during the marriage did you and your former spouse cohabit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did we cohabit long enough for a division after a divorce or annulment between 1978 and 1987` IF
    `s 55(2)(a) — the former spouses cohabited for at least thirty-six consecutive months during the marriage` `the number of consecutive months during the marriage that we cohabited`

-- s 55(2)(b). On what day the marriage is deemed solemnized or nullified, or a divorce made final: the last day of the year before the year of the registered date.
@export On what day is my marriage deemed solemnized, nullified or my divorce deemed made final (s 55(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the registered date of the marriage, or the registered date of the judgment of nullity, or the effective date of the judgment granting a divorce` IS A DATE @desc What is the registered date of the marriage, or of the judgment of nullity, or the effective date of the judgment granting the divorce?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my marriage deemed solemnized, nullified or my divorce deemed made final` IS
    `s 55(2)(b) — the day on which the marriage is deemed solemnized or nullified or a divorce is deemed made final` `the registered date of the marriage, or the registered date of the judgment of nullity, or the effective date of the judgment granting a divorce`

-- s 55(2)(c). Whether we are deemed to have cohabited during a year: deemed to have in the year of the marriage, deemed not to have in the year of the divorce or annulment.
@export Are we deemed to have cohabited during a year (s 55(2)(c))?
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Which year are you asking about?
      `the year in which the marriage was solemnized` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year was the marriage solemnized?
      `the year of the divorce or of the annulment of the marriage` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year was the divorce or the annulment of the marriage?
      `we actually cohabited during the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you and your former spouse actually cohabit during the year?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are we deemed to have cohabited during a year` IF
    `s 55(2)(c) — the former spouses are deemed to have cohabited during a year` `the year` `the year in which the marriage was solemnized` `the year of the divorce or of the annulment of the marriage` `we actually cohabited during the year`

-- s 55(4). On the Minister's approval, each former spouse is attributed half of the sum of their unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation.
@export What is attributed to me when the Minister approves a division after a divorce or annulment between 1978 and 1987 (s 55(4))?
GIVEN `the Minister has approved the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved the application?
      `my unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to contributions made under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to contributions under the Act, in dollars (worked out as section 78 sets out)?
      `my former spouse's unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to contributions made under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your former spouse's unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to contributions under the Act, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is attributed to me when the Minister approves a division after a divorce or annulment between 1978 and 1987` IS
    `s 55(4) — the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to each former spouse on a division` `the Minister has approved the application` `my unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to contributions made under the Act` `my former spouse's unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to contributions made under the Act`

-- s 55(5). Where there is a division under the Act and under a provincial plan, the contributor's total for the year is the sum.
@export What are my total unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year of division under the Act and a provincial pension plan (s 55(5))?
GIVEN `the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me under subsection 55(4)` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was attributed to you under subsection 55(4), in dollars?
      `the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was attributed to you under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my total unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year of division under the Act and a provincial pension plan` IS
    `s 55(5) — the total unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division under this Act and a provincial pension plan` `the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me under subsection 55(4)` `the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me under a provincial pension plan`

-- s 55(6). A division is made for a month unless the couple's total earnings in the year do not exceed twice the Year's Basic Exemption, the month is before either reached 18 or after either reached 70, either was receiving a retirement pension, or the month is excluded for disability.
@export Is a division made for a month of our period of cohabitation (s 55(6))?
GIVEN `the month` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (Any date in that month.)
      `our total unadjusted pensionable earnings in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your and your former spouse's total unadjusted pensionable earnings in the year, in dollars?
      `the Year's Basic Exemption` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Year's Basic Exemption for the year, in dollars?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `my former spouse's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your former spouse's date of birth?
      `I was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under the Act or a provincial pension plan in the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a beneficiary of a retirement pension under the Act or a provincial pension plan in the month?
      `my former spouse was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under the Act or a provincial pension plan in the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your former spouse a beneficiary of a retirement pension under the Act or a provincial pension plan in the month?
      `the month is excluded from my contributory period by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the month excluded from your contributory period, under the Act or a provincial pension plan, by reason of disability?
      `the month is excluded from my former spouse's contributory period by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the month excluded from your former spouse's contributory period, under the Act or a provincial pension plan, by reason of disability?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a division made for a month of our period of cohabitation` IF
    `s 55(6) — a division is made for a month of the period of cohabitation` `the month` `our total unadjusted pensionable earnings in the year` `the Year's Basic Exemption` `my date of birth` `my former spouse's date of birth` `I was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under the Act or a provincial pension plan in the month` `my former spouse was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under the Act or a provincial pension plan in the month` `the month is excluded from my contributory period by reason of disability` `the month is excluded from my former spouse's contributory period by reason of disability`

-- s 55(7). Where a benefit is already payable, it is recalculated and paid from the month after the application was received.
@export From which month will my benefit be paid at the amount recalculated for a division (s 55(7))?
GIVEN `the application has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the application for a division been approved?
      `a benefit is payable to me or in respect of me or my former spouse for a month commencing on or before the day the application was received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a benefit payable to or in respect of either of you for a month commencing on or before the day the application was received?
      `the day the application was received` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the application received?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which month will my benefit be paid at the amount recalculated for a division` IS
    `s 55(7) — the month from which the benefit adjusted for the division is paid` `the application has been approved` `a benefit is payable to me or in respect of me or my former spouse for a month commencing on or before the day the application was received` `the day the application was received`

-- s 55(8). The paired duty: on approval, the applicant and the former spouse or their estate must be notified; a person dissatisfied may appeal.
@export Am I to be notified when a division is approved (s 55(8))?
GIVEN `the Minister has approved an application for division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved an application for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I to be notified when a division is approved` IF
    `s 55(8) — the applicant and the former spouse or the former spouse's estate must be notified of the approval` `the Minister has approved an application for division of unadjusted pensionable earnings`

@export Do I have a right of appeal against a division (s 55(8))?
GIVEN `the Minister has approved an application for division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved an application for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings?
      `I am dissatisfied with the division or the result of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, as the applicant or the former spouse (or the estate), dissatisfied with the division or the result of it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a right of appeal against a division` IF
    `s 55(8) — an applicant or a former spouse who is dissatisfied with the division has the right of appeal` `the Minister has approved an application for division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` `I am dissatisfied with the division or the result of it`

§§ `Dividing earnings with a former spouse or partner: divorce, separation and the end of a common-law partnership (sections 55.1 to 55.2)`

-- s 55.1(1)(a). A divorce or nullity judgment, once the Minister has been informed and has the prescribed information, divides the earnings of the spouses without an application.
@export Will my earnings be divided on my divorce or the annulment of my marriage (s 55.1(1)(a))?
GIVEN `a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of the marriage has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a judgment granting a divorce, or a judgment of nullity of the marriage, been given?
      `the Minister has been informed of the judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister been informed of the judgment?
      `the Minister has received the prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister received the prescribed information?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my earnings be divided on my divorce or the annulment of my marriage` IF
    `s 55.1(1)(a) — a division takes place on a judgment granting a divorce or of nullity of the marriage` `a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of the marriage has been given` `the Minister has been informed of the judgment` `the Minister has received the prescribed information`

-- s 55.1(1)(b). Spouses living separate and apart for a year or more may have their earnings divided on application; where one has died, the application must be made within three years after the death.
@export Can my earnings be divided on application because my spouse and I live separate and apart (s 55.1(1)(b))?
GIVEN `we are spouses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and the other person spouses (married to each other)?
      `the Minister has approved an application made by or on behalf of either of us, by the estate or succession of either, or by a person who may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved an application made by or on behalf of either of you, by the estate or succession of either, or by a person who may be prescribed?
      `the day we commenced to live separate and apart` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you commence to live separate and apart?
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is (or was) the application made?
      `one of us has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has one of you died?
      `the day one of us died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did one of you die? (Any date if neither has.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my earnings be divided on application because my spouse and I live separate and apart` IF
    `s 55.1(1)(b) — a division takes place on the approval of an application by spouses living separate and apart` `we are spouses` `the Minister has approved an application made by or on behalf of either of us, by the estate or succession of either, or by a person who may be prescribed` `the day we commenced to live separate and apart` `the day the application is made` (IF `one of us has died` THEN JUST `the day one of us died` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 55.1(1)(c). Former common-law partners living separate and apart for a year or more (or one has died during that period) may have their earnings divided on application made within four years, or later if both agree in writing.
@export Can my earnings be divided on application because my common-law partner and I have separated (s 55.1(1)(c))?
GIVEN `we are former common-law partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and the other person former common-law partners?
      `the Minister has approved an application made by or on behalf of either of us, by the estate or succession of one of us, or by a person who may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved an application made by or on behalf of either of you, by the estate or succession of one of you, or by a person who may be prescribed?
      `the day we commenced to live separate and apart` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you commence to live separate and apart?
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is (or was) the application made?
      `one of us died during the period of living separate and apart` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did one of you die during the period of living separate and apart?
      `the day one of us died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did one of you die? (Any date if neither did.)
      `we both agree in writing to an application made at any time after the end of the four-year period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you both agree in writing to an application made at any time after the end of the four-year period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my earnings be divided on application because my common-law partner and I have separated` IF
    `s 55.1(1)(c) — a division takes place on the approval of an application by former common-law partners living separate and apart` `we are former common-law partners` `the Minister has approved an application made by or on behalf of either of us, by the estate or succession of one of us, or by a person who may be prescribed` `the day we commenced to live separate and apart` `the day the application is made` (IF `one of us died during the period of living separate and apart` THEN JUST `the day one of us died` ELSE NOTHING) `we both agree in writing to an application made at any time after the end of the four-year period`

-- s 55.1(2)(a). Whether we are deemed to have lived separate and apart for a period: we lived apart during it and either of us intended to.
@export Are we deemed to have lived separate and apart for a period (s 55.1(2)(a))?
GIVEN `we lived apart during the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you live apart during the period?
      `either of us had the intention to live separate and apart from the other during the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did either of you have the intention to live separate and apart from the other during the period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are we deemed to have lived separate and apart for a period` IF
    `s 55.1(2)(a) — the persons are deemed to have lived separate and apart for a period` `we lived apart during the period` `either of us had the intention to live separate and apart from the other during the period`

-- s 55.1(2)(b). Our separation is not considered interrupted or ended by either of us becoming incapable (if the Minister thinks it would have continued) or by a resumed cohabitation of 90 days or fewer in total with reconciliation as its primary purpose.
@export Is our separation treated as continuing despite an interruption (s 55.1(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the only reason for the interruption is that either of us became incapable of forming or having an intention to continue to live separate and apart or of continuing to live separate and apart of our own volition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason for the interruption that either of you became incapable of forming or having an intention to continue to live separate and apart, or of continuing to live apart of your own volition?
      `it appears to the Minister that the separation would probably have continued had that person not become so incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Minister that the separation would probably have continued had that person not become so incapable?
      `the only reason for the interruption is that we resumed cohabitation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason for the interruption that you resumed cohabitation?
      `the total days of resumed cohabitation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in total did you resume cohabitation?
      `reconciliation was the primary purpose of the resumed cohabitation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was reconciliation the primary purpose of the resumed cohabitation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our separation treated as continuing despite an interruption` IF
    `s 55.1(2)(b) — a period of living separate and apart is not considered to have been interrupted or terminated` `the only reason for the interruption is that either of us became incapable of forming or having an intention to continue to live separate and apart or of continuing to live separate and apart of our own volition` `it appears to the Minister that the separation would probably have continued had that person not become so incapable` `the only reason for the interruption is that we resumed cohabitation` `the total days of resumed cohabitation` `reconciliation was the primary purpose of the resumed cohabitation`

-- s 55.1(3). For a division, we must have cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year, determined in the manner prescribed by regulation (regulation 78.1).
@export Did we cohabit for a continuous period of at least one year (s 55.1(3))?
GIVEN `we cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year, determined in a manner prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cohabit for a continuous period of at least one year, determined in the manner prescribed by regulation (regulation 78.1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did we cohabit for a continuous period of at least one year` IF
    `s 55.1(3) — the persons subject to a division cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year` `we cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year, determined in a manner prescribed by regulation`

-- s 55.1(5). The Minister's power, which is my liability: before a division is made, or within the prescribed period after, the Minister may refuse to make it, or cancel it, if benefits are payable to or in respect of both of us and both would decrease.
@export Can the Minister refuse to make or cancel my division because both our benefits would decrease (s 55.1(5))?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that benefits are payable to or in respect of both of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that benefits are payable to or in respect of both of you?
      `the Minister is satisfied that the amount of both benefits decreased at the time the division was made or would decrease at the time the division was proposed to be made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the amount of both benefits decreased when the division was made, or would decrease when it is proposed to be made?
      `the division has not yet been made, or it was made within the prescribed period before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the division not yet been made, or was it made within the prescribed period before?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Minister refuse to make or cancel my division because both our benefits would decrease` IF
    `s 55.1(5) — the Minister may refuse to make or may cancel a division` `the Minister is satisfied that benefits are payable to or in respect of both of us` `the Minister is satisfied that the amount of both benefits decreased at the time the division was made or would decrease at the time the division was proposed to be made` `the division has not yet been made, or it was made within the prescribed period before`

-- s 55.1. Whether a division takes place at all: one of paragraphs (1)(a), (b) and (c) is met, we cohabited a continuous year, no agreement binds the Minister, and the Minister has not refused or cancelled.
@export Does a division of my earnings take place under section 55.1 (s 55.1)?
GIVEN `a division takes place under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a division take place on a divorce or annulment (see that question)?
      `a division takes place under paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a division take place on application by spouses living separate and apart (see that question)?
      `a division takes place under paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a division take place on application by former common-law partners living separate and apart (see that question)?
      `we cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cohabit for a continuous period of at least one year (see that question)?
      `a written agreement binds the Minister under subsection 55.2(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written agreement bind the Minister under subsection 55.2(3), so that the Minister shall not make a division (see that question)?
      `the Minister has refused to make or has cancelled the division under subsection 55.1(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister refused to make, or cancelled, the division under subsection 55.1(5)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a division of my earnings take place under section 55.1` IF
    `s 55.1 — a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings takes place` `a division takes place under paragraph (1)(a)` `a division takes place under paragraph (1)(b)` `a division takes place under paragraph (1)(c)` `we cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year` `a written agreement binds the Minister under subsection 55.2(3)` `the Minister has refused to make or has cancelled the division under subsection 55.1(5)`

-- s 55.11. Which cases section 55.1 reaches: judgments of divorce or nullity on or after 1 January 1987; spouses who began to live apart on or after 1 January 1987 and before the section came into force; spouses and former common-law partners who began to live apart after it.
@export Does section 55.1 apply to my case (s 55.11)?
GIVEN `there was a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of the marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a judgment granting a divorce, or a judgment of nullity of the marriage?
      `the day of that judgment` IS A DATE @desc On what day was that judgment given? (Any date if there was none.)
      `we commenced to live separate and apart` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commence to live separate and apart?
      `the day we commenced to live separate and apart` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you commence to live separate and apart? (Any date if you did not.)
      `we are spouses or former spouses, in the sense the word spouse had immediately before the section came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you spouses or former spouses, in the sense the word spouse had immediately before section 55.11 came into force (married to each other)?
      `we are spouses or former common-law partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you spouses or former common-law partners?
      `the day section 55.11 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 55.11 come into force? (The text of the Act does not give the day.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 55.1 apply to my case` IF
    `s 55.11 — section 55.1 applies to the case` (IF `there was a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of the marriage` THEN JUST `the day of that judgment` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `we commenced to live separate and apart` THEN JUST `the day we commenced to live separate and apart` ELSE NOTHING) `we are spouses or former spouses, in the sense the word spouse had immediately before the section came into force` `we are spouses or former common-law partners` `the day section 55.11 came into force`

-- s 55.2(2). The provisions of a written agreement between us, or of a court order, made on or after 4 June 1986 do not bind the Minister in a division, except as subsection (3) provides.
-- The answer is yes only for an agreement or order of that date that subsection (3) does not rescue; for one made earlier the subsection says nothing.
@export Does the Act say that our agreement or a court order made on or after June 4, 1986 does not bind the Minister in a division (s 55.2(2))?
GIVEN `we made a written agreement, or a court made an order, on or after June 4, 1986` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a written agreement, or did a court make an order, on or after June 4, 1986?
      `subsection 55.2(3) makes the provision of our agreement binding on the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 55.2(3) make the provision of your agreement binding on the Minister (see that question)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act say that our agreement or a court order made on or after June 4, 1986 does not bind the Minister in a division` IF
    `s 55.2(2) — an agreement or court order does not bind the Minister in a division` `we made a written agreement, or a court made an order, on or after June 4, 1986` `subsection 55.2(3) makes the provision of our agreement binding on the Minister`

-- s 55.2(3). A provision of a written agreement made on or after 4 June 1986 saying that there is to be no division, expressly mentioning the Act, binds the Minister, who shall not divide, if provincial law expressly permits it, it was made before the application (or before the judgment), and no court has invalidated it.
@export Does our agreement that there be no division bind the Minister (s 55.2(3))?
GIVEN `we made a written agreement on or after June 4, 1986` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a written agreement on or after June 4, 1986?
      `the agreement contains a provision that expressly mentions the Act and says there is to be no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement contain a provision that expressly mentions the Canada Pension Plan Act and says that there is to be no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1?
      `that provision is expressly permitted under the provincial law that governs such agreements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that provision expressly permitted under the provincial law that governs such agreements?
      `the division is under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the division be under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) (on an application)?
      `the division is under paragraph 55.1(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the division be under paragraph 55.1(1)(a) (on a divorce or annulment)?
      `the day we made the agreement` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make the agreement?
      `the day of the application for the division` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the application for the division made? (Any date if the division is under paragraph 55.1(1)(a).)
      `the day of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the judgment granting the divorce, or of nullity of the marriage, rendered? (Any date if the division is on an application.)
      `that provision has not been invalidated by a court order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that provision not been invalidated by a court order?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our agreement that there be no division bind the Minister` IF
    `s 55.2(3) — a provision of an agreement is binding on the Minister and the Minister shall not make a division` `we made a written agreement on or after June 4, 1986` `the agreement contains a provision that expressly mentions the Act and says there is to be no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1` `that provision is expressly permitted under the provincial law that governs such agreements` `the division is under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c)` `the division is under paragraph 55.1(1)(a)` `the day we made the agreement` `the day of the application for the division` `the day of the judgment granting a divorce or the judgment of nullity of the marriage` `that provision has not been invalidated by a court order`

-- s 55.2(4). The paired duty: the Minister must notify each person subject to the division, without delay, once informed of the judgment or on receiving an application.
@export Must I be notified without delay of a division (s 55.2(4))?
GIVEN `the Minister has been informed of a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of a marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister been informed of a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of a marriage?
      `the Minister has received an application under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister received an application under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be notified without delay of a division` IF
    `s 55.2(4) — each person subject to the division must be notified without delay` `the Minister has been informed of a judgment granting a divorce or a judgment of nullity of a marriage` `the Minister has received an application under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c)`

-- s 55.2(5). On a division under section 55.1, each person is attributed half of the sum of their base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation.
@export What base earnings are attributed to me on a division under section 55.1 (s 55.2(5))?
GIVEN `there is a division under section 55.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a division under section 55.1?
      `my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions made under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions under the Act, in dollars (worked out as section 78 sets out)?
      `my former partner's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions made under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your former spouse's or partner's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions under the Act, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What base earnings are attributed to me on a division under section 55.1` IS
    `s 55.2(5) — the base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to each person on a division under section 55.1` `there is a division under section 55.1` `my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions made under the Act` `my former partner's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to base contributions made under the Act`

-- s 55.2(5.1). The same for the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings.
@export What first additional earnings are attributed to me on a division under section 55.1 (s 55.2(5.1))?
GIVEN `there is a division under section 55.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a division under section 55.1?
      `my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to first additional contributions made under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to first additional contributions under the Act, in dollars (worked out as section 78.1 sets out)?
      `my former partner's first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to first additional contributions made under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your former spouse's or partner's first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to first additional contributions under the Act, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What first additional earnings are attributed to me on a division under section 55.1` IS
    `s 55.2(5.1) — the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to each person on a division under section 55.1` `there is a division under section 55.1` `my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to first additional contributions made under the Act` `my former partner's first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the period of cohabitation attributable to first additional contributions made under the Act`
